          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Condition-Monitoring Records\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nThis report analyzes 18 condition-monitoring records spanning five equipment classes (valves, turbines, pipelines, separators, pumps, compressors, heat exchangers, a reactor, and a condenser) across 17 stations. Each record contains five measured parameters: pressure (kPa), temperature (\u00b0C), flow (m\u00b3/h), vibration (mm/s RMS), and efficiency (%).\n\nThree findings warrant immediate attention:\n\n1. **Two units exhibit severe vibration**: turbine 3108 (8.9 mm/s) and heat exchanger 7102 (8.7 mm/s). Per ISO 10816-3 vibration severity zones, anything above 7.1 mm/s on medium-sized machines falls in **Zone D (\"vibration normally unacceptable for continuous operation\")**, placing these units at high risk of imminent failure.\n2. **One unit shows a severe flow deficit**: pump 4373 at station 279 records only 32 m\u00b3/h against a fleet-typical range of 197\u2013856 m\u00b3/h. This is consistent with suction starvation, a closed/blocked discharge, severe impeller wear, or a large internal recirculation",
